    {
      "id": "p0074-b008",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Naturally, from an outsider's perspective - and from a paying client's perspective - leaving text untranslated might seem like the mark of a shoddy translator. But when translating a game from English into Japanese, it can actually be the mark of an experienced translator.",
        "raw": "Naturally, from an outsider's perspective - and from a paying client's\nperspective - leaving text untranslated might seem like the mark of a shoddy\ntranslator. But when translating a game from English into Japanese, it can\nactually be the mark of an experienced translator.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29780907,
          0.63885,
          0.88079308,
          0.70617857
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.28735323,
          0.63813571,
          0.89924278,
          0.70725
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          22,
          23,
          25,
          26
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "从圈外人，尤其是付钱的客户看来，不翻译某些文字也许像是译者粗制滥造。但游戏从英语译成日语时，这反而可能说明译者经验丰富。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
      "annotations": [],
      "layout": {
