    {
      "id": "p0074-b009",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "When Undertale’s title must be written in Japanese for whatever reason, the official Japanese spelling is アンダーテイル (“andāteiru”). Prior to the official Japanese release, fans used the slightly different spelling of アンダーテール (“andātēru”). The game’s new, official spelling was one of many ways in which the official Japanese release initially seemed “off” to early fans.",
        "raw": "When Underta/e's title must be written in Japanese for whatever reason, the\nofficial Japanese spelling is 7 YY· '- f-1 Jv (\"andateirn\"). Prior to the official\nJapanese release, fans used the slightly different spelling of 7 /'5'\"- 7-- ;i,\n(\"andateru\"). The game's new, official spelling was one of many ways in which\nthe official Japanese release initially seemed \"off\" to early fans.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en",
          "ja"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29726197,
          0.81196429,
          0.89109695,
          0.89705
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.28735323,
          0.81125,
          0.89924278,
          0.89812143
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          34,
          35,
          36,
          37,
          38
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "如果由于某种原因必须用日文写游戏名，官方写法是アンダーテイル（andāteiru，Undertale 的音译）。官方日语版出现以前，玩家用的写法略有不同，是アンダーテール（andātēru，同一游戏名的另一种音译）。新的官方写法，也是早期玩家最初觉得官方译版“不对劲”的诸多地方之一。",
        "status": "draft",
